    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents are delighted to bring to the market this exceptional residential farm holding occupying a peaceful and picturesque setting in the heart of Connemara. Extending to approximately 5.76 hectares (14.23 acres), together with valuable commonage rights over approximately 23.92 hectares (59.10 acres), the property combines a beautifully maintained three-bedroom detached residence, productive grazing lands, an extensive range of agricultural buildings and significant commonage rights to create an outstanding holding of exceptional quality and versatility.Complete holdings of this nature seldom come to the market. Surrounded by the breath-taking landscapes that have made Connemara one of Ireland's most sought-after destinations, the property offers an exceptional balance of comfortable family living and practical agricultural infrastructure. Whether continuing a farming tradition, establishing a hobby farm or simply embracing the peace, privacy and freedom of country living, this is a property that offers endless possibilities.At the heart of the holding sits a beautifully presented three-bedroom detached residence, thoughtfully designed for modern family living and presented in excellent condition throughout. The bright and spacious accommodation comprises a welcoming sitting room with an attractive open fireplace, a well-appointed fitted kitchen, an impressive open-plan living and dining room centred around a traditional Stanley Range, three generous double bedrooms including a master en-suite, and a family bathroom. Warm, inviting and ready for immediate occupation, the home enjoys delightful views across its surrounding lands and perfectly complements its idyllic rural setting.The adjoining lands extend to approximately 5.76 hectares (14.23 acres) and are complemented by an excellent range of domestic and agricultural outbuildings. The holding is exceptionally well equipped, benefiting from a substantial farmyard, traditional cattle accommodation, storage buildings, a large detached garage and livestock handling facilities, providing excellent infrastructure for a wide variety of farming enterprises while equally appealing to those seeking a substantial lifestyle property.A particularly valuable feature of the holding is the inclusion of extensive commonage rights extending to approximately 23.92 hectares (59.10 acres). The property benefits from a 1/36th undivided share in three separate commonage areas, including approximately 22.52 hectares (55.62 acres) of quality hill grazing adjoining the main holding, together with additional commonage interests extending to approximately 1.34 hectares (3.31 acres) and 0.06 hectares (0.16 acres) respectively. Commonage rights of this scale are increasingly difficult to acquire and significantly enhance both the agricultural appeal and long-term value of this exceptional property.The property is just 14km from Oughterard, affectionately known as the Gateway to Connemara. The village offers an excellent range of amenities including supermarkets, cafés, award-winning restaurants, traditional pubs, schools, medical services, pharmacies, sporting facilities and boutique shops. Renowned for its world-class trout and salmon fishing on Lough Corrib, championship golf course and spectacular scenery, Oughterard perfectly balances village charm with an outstanding outdoor lifestyle. The nearby villages of Costelloe, Rossaveal and Carraroe provide further amenities and access to the stunning Connemara coastline, while Galway City is approximately 42km away.Offering a beautifully maintained family home, quality grazing lands, excellent agricultural infrastructure and extensive commonage rights, Shannapheasteen represents a unique opportunity to acquire a complete Connemara holding in one of the West of Ireland's most scenic and unspoilt locations."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - \nA welcoming entrance leading into the main hallway.\n\nEntrance Hall - \nBright and spacious hallway with carpet flooring, cloak storage and access to the principal accommodation.\n\nLiving / Dining Room - \nA warm and inviting reception room featuring decorative ceiling coving and an attractive open fireplace, creating the perfect setting for relaxing with family and friends.\n\nKitchen - \nWell-appointed fitted kitchen with tiled flooring, generous worktop space, fitted units, gas hob, electric oven and direct access to the rear of the property.\n\nLiving Room - \nA bright and spacious open-plan living and dining area centred around a traditional Stanley Range, with patio doors opening to the rear, creating a wonderful space for everyday family living and entertaining.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nA generous front-facing double bedroom complete with built-in wardrobes and pleasant views across the surrounding countryside.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nAnother spacious front-facing double bedroom offering bright and comfortable accommodation, ideal for family members or guests.\n\nMaster Bedroom - \nA generously proportioned rear-facing double bedroom with built-in wardrobes and a fully tiled ensuite shower room, creating a peaceful private retreat overlooking the surrounding lands.\n\nEnsuite - \nFully tiled and fitted with shower, wash hand basin and WC.\n\nFamily Bathroom - \nWell-appointed bathroom complete with bath, wash hand basin and WC.\n\nLarge Detached Garage - \n\n\nStorage Sheds - \n\n\nTraditional Cattle Shed - \n\n\nWell Maintained Farmyard - \n\n\nCattle Crush & Livestock Handling Facilities - \n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Rare opportunity to acquire a complete Connemara holding</li><li> Approx. 5.76 hectares (14.23 acres) of adjoining grazing lands</li><li> Approx. 23.92 hectares (59.10 acres) of valuable commonage rights</li><li> Beautifully maintained three-bedroom detached residence</li><li> Excellent range of farm buildings and agricultural infrastructure</li><li> Traditional farmyard with livestock handling facilities</li><li> Ideal for farming, equestrian or countryside living</li><li> Solar panels, oil-fired central heating & double-glazed windows</li><li> Peaceful yet convenient location close to Oughterard and Galway City</ul>"
